Open S3 and click “Create bucket.” 
Enter any bucket name, then scroll down and click “Create bucket.” 
 
Go to the bucket and click the “Upload” option. 


Click “Add files,” select an image from your computer, and then click “Upload.”  
 
When you open the image, you will see this page. Some configurations are still pending. 
Go to the bucket, select your bucket, click the “Permissions” tab, and then edit “Block public access.”  
Uncheck “Block all public access” and then click “Save changes.” 
Click “Bucket policy” and then click “Edit.”
 
Then open the AWS Policy Generator. 
Policy Type: Select S3 Bucket Policy. 
Principal: Enter *. 
Actions: Select All Actions. 
ARN: Paste the ARN shown on the Bucket Policy page. 
Click “Add Statement” and then click “Generate Policy.” 
 






Copy the generated policy. 
Paste the generated policy into the “Bucket policy” editor. Then edit item 9 by changing the “Resource” value to:
"Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::mohantyabhishek123/*"
 

Then scroll down and click “Save changes.” 
